cept is extended to nicely edge distance-balanced and strongly edge distance-balanced graphs revealing significant outcomes.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nON SOME PROPERTIES OF QUASI-DISTANCE-BALANCED GRAPHS (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/322800453_ON_SOME_PROPERTIES_OF_QUASI-DISTANCE-BALANCED_GRAPHS)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Abedi, M. ... Kutnar, Quasi-λ-distance-balanced graphs, Dis- ... distance-balanced graphs and graph products, European J.\nLemma 4.1 it follows that G is isomorphic to a star. Let x∈V(G 2)\\ {v 2}. It is now easy to see\n\nthat |W G\n\nv 2,x| ≥ |V(G 1)|+ 1, and that |W G\n\nx,v 2| ≤ |V(G 2)| − 1. It is also clear that |W G\n\nv 2,x|≥|W G\n\nx,v 2|,\n\nimplying that |W G\n\nv 2,x|=λ|W G\n\nx,v 2|, that is\n\nλ=|W G\n\nv 2,x|\n\n|W G\n\nx,v 2|≥|V(G 1)|+ 1\n\n|V(G 2)| − 1>|V(G 1)|\n\n|V(G 2)|=λ,\n\na contradiction. The obtained contradiction shows that a quasi-DB graph with a bridge is iso-\n\nmorphic to a star.\n\nThe next natural question is the characterization of quasi-DB graphs with a cut-vertex. As\n\nAcknowledgement\n\nThis work is supported in part by the Slovenian Research Agency (research program P1-0285 and\n\nresearch projects N1-0032, N1-0038, N1-0062, and J1-7051).\n\n8\n\nReferences\n\n[1] A. Abedi, M. Alaeiyan, A. Hujdurovi´c, K. Kutnar, Quasi-λ-distance-balanced graphs, Dis-\n\ncrete Appl. Math.,227 (2017), 21-28.\n\n[2] K. Balakrishnan, M. Changat, I. Peterin, S. ˇ\n\nSpacapan, P. ˇ\n\nSparl, A. R. Subhamathi, Strongly\n\ndistance-balanced graphs and graph products, European J. Combin. 30 (2009), 1048-1053.\n\n[3] N. Biggs, Algebraic graph theory, second edition, Cambridge University Press (1993).\n\n[4] S. Cabello, P. Lukˇsiˇc, The complexity of obtaining a distance-balanced graph, Electron. J.\n\nCombin. 18 (1) (2011) Paper 49.\n\n[5] D. ˇ\n\nZ. Djokovi´c, Distance-preserving subgraphs of hypercubes, J. Comb